          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since this action removes the factor 11 in the LHS, we can write this step as:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.439,
            0.127,
            0.555,
            0.146
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_2.jpg",
          "content": "y = 66 \\div 11."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.15,
            0.847,
            0.19
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Again, we could have arrived at this by seeing multiplication and division as inverse operations, as in the case of Example 2."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.193,
            0.742,
            0.214
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us write down both these ways of solving an equation."
            }
